# Tests (Minitest)

- Scope: authoring `test/**/*.rb` — structure, naming, assertions (not CI wiring).
- Identificadores de produção em setup/helpers → `naming-rails.mdc`. Nomes de teste (frase legível) → abaixo.
- Each case **short** and proves **one** outcome. Name is **human sentence** (product person readable): scenario + expectation — not `test_calls_foo`.
- Stack: `ActiveSupport::TestCase`, `ActionDispatch::IntegrationTest`, etc. Prefer `test "…" do` or `def test_*` — not RSpec DSL unless project already uses `minitest/spec`.
- TDD: RED → GREEN → REFACTOR; do not change prod + assertions in same step when proving behavior.
- One behavior cluster per test method; unrelated expectations → split files / tests.
- No `sleep` — deterministic waits/assertions.
- Time: `travel_to` / `freeze_time` — not bare `Time.now` in assertions setup.
- Test **public** API — no `send(:private_method)`.
- File layout: `test/**` mirrors `app/**`; file `*_test.rb` per class under test.
- System tests: critical flows only (slow); default unit/integration.
- HTTP: WebMock / VCR — no real network in CI.
- Order: rely on Minitest random order — never `i_suck_and_my_tests_are_order_dependent!`.
- Fixtures **xor** factories per project convention — not both mixed without reason.
- `setup` data not shared across unrelated tests.
- Mock/stub **external** boundaries (HTTP, mail, queue, clock, RNG) — not your own application classes.
- State deltas → `assert_difference` / `assert_changes` instead of manual before/after juggling when fit.
- Migrations: **no contract tests** — do not add specs that mirror `db/migrate` (columns, indexes, FKs, `up`/`down`). Schema is the migration + `schema.rb`; prove effects through model/query/integration behavior.

```ruby
# bad: test "works" do … multiple unrelated asserts … end
# good: test "rejects checkout when stock is zero" do … one scenario … end
```
